-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Mad Mix 2 - en el Castillo de los Fantasmas
  Publisher   Topo Soft, 1990
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Mad Mix 2 - en el Castillo de los Fantasmas (1990)(Topo
              Soft)(128K)(ES).z80
  MD5         f5f5262f7a41d3c55408b45878c31d00

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 colours as the set has them, the whole picture and
              the panel, stages 1 to 3. Stages 4 to 9 stay as the original.
              Source: Enhanced colours: Jao Paulo (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the copy to the screen no longer writes port 0xFF, which on
              a Next is Timex hi-colour; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe; the game takes random numbers from ROM
              bytes); the tape's loading screen; three tested options;
              Enhanced colours, a menu option, off by default, from the
              Spec256 set by Jao Paulo, as they are: the whole play window on
              a double-buffered Layer 2, flipped in the top border, with the
              original still running and on the ULA underneath; each original
              routine's exact time kept

  Note        Keys: T fire and start, R up, C down, D left, F right, P pause
              (any key resumes), V music on or off. Options: Kempston
              joystick, or Q A O P Space (T then pauses). Default: the
              original look, no clash to remove. Enhanced (off): the Spec256
              colours, the whole picture and the panel on Layer 2, stages 1 to
              3. Known issues: pace in JNext, Enhanced, +0.09 to +0.26%
              against the original over 800 updates, 5 seeds; quiet thirds
              +0.02 to +0.38%, busy thirds +0.07 to +0.26%; slowest 20 updates
              +2.95%. Enhanced is original colours in stages 4 to 9 (the set
              holds only the first three), on the menus, the STAGE screen, the
              game over screen. The set's READY box keeps the screen's blue.
              Missing: colours for stages 4 to 9; natural play past stage 1
              (stages by a test copy); hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Kempston joystick
   3  Keys Q A O P space

  The archive's Infinite lives for this release, tested alone in the
  simulator, 3 seeds x 7,000 frames, same keys with and without it: none lost
  against 1, 4 and 5. Kempston joystick (the game's own mode 2) and Q A O P
  Space (the game's key table): tested the same way, 3 seeds; without the
  option those inputs do nothing.

