-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy; 1.0 not yet played by the owner; published at his request

  Replay      Default: unchanged from 1.0, byte for byte (40067 frames
              IDENTICAL). Enhanced: 4 scripted recordings, 70074 frames,
              133046 hooks run original and build from one state: every
              register including R, all RAM but the changed bytes and the
              stack below SP, clock, MMU and write map: IDENTICAL; 4163
              pictures, 115098624 pixels, against an independent model, after
              every hook and every flip; 14 broken builds caught; 402 cases of
              the handler interrupting a hook: picture and RAM as without it;
              the start-up exact with and without NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, default, Enhanced and with the
              cheat, output byte for byte as nxc.py makes it, reaching play;
              15-minute soak of Enhanced against the original; flicker check
              clean; every flip outside the 192 screen rows

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: stage 1 with deaths, game over
              and a new game; all 9 stages through a test copy that ends a
              stage at its first pill; not reached: natural completion

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
